@* The drawer/appbar shell is a constant dark olive in BOTH light and dark mode (see MainLayout's
   theme), so nav text must read against --mud-palette-drawer-text/-icon (the shell's own light
   text tokens) — NOT --mud-palette-text-primary, which flips dark in light mode and would be
   unreadable against the still-dark sidebar. Active item gets a gold accent bar, matching the
   approved "Ledger" design's one deliberate secondary accent. *@
<style>
    .mud-navmenu .mud-nav-link,
    .mud-navmenu .mud-nav-group > .mud-nav-link {
        color: var(--mud-palette-drawer-text);
        font-weight: 500;
        opacity: 1;
    }
    .mud-navmenu .mud-nav-link .mud-nav-link-icon {
        color: var(--mud-palette-drawer-icon);
    }
    .mud-navmenu .mud-nav-link.active {
        color: #f3e6cf !important;
        background-color: rgba(146, 102, 44, 0.18);
        font-weight: 700;
        box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--brand-gold, #92662c);
    }
    .mud-navmenu .mud-nav-link.active .mud-nav-link-icon {
        color: var(--brand-gold, #92662c);
    }
    .mud-navmenu .mud-nav-link:hover {
        background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    }
</style>
